/section></div><div class="evidence-floor"><section class="network-panel"><div class="panel-label">EVIDENCE NETWORK // INTERACTIVE MODEL</div><div class="network" id="network"><span class="claim-node">CLAIM</span><button style="--x:14%;--y:28%" data-tip="Primary records">P</button><button style="--x:30%;--y:70%" data-tip="Independent reporting">R</button><button style="--x:52%;--y:18%" data-tip="Historical record">H</button><button style="--x:72%;--y:67%" data-tip="Counterevidence">C</button><button style="--x:88%;--y:28%" data-tip="Later analysis">A</button><svg viewBox="0 0 100 50" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M50 25 L14 14 M50 25 L30 35 M50 25 L52 9 M50 25 L72 34 M50 25 L88 14"/></svg><output id="nodeTip">Select an evidence node to inspect its role.</output></div></section><section class="findings-panel"><div class="panel-label">EVIDENTIARY STATES</div><ul class="findings"><li class="yes"><b>VERIFIED FACT</b><span>Documented relationships and covert media activity existed.</span></li><li class="warn"><b>INFERENCE</b><span>Documented activity does not automatically establish total control.</span></li><li class="info"><b>MISSING CONTEXT</b><span>Scope, time period, institutional boundaries and definitions matter.</span></li><li class="unknown"><b>UNKNOWN</b><span>Claims about present-day total control require present-day evidence.</span></li></ul></section></div></article></div></section><section class="section protocol"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">ANALYST PROTOCOL</div><h2>Every conclusion has to survive contact with its evidence.</h2></div></div><div class="protocol-grid"><article class="glass tilt"><b>01</b><h3>TRACE ORIGIN</h3><p>Move toward primary and earliest accessible evidence instead of treating repetition as corroboration.</p></article><article class="glass tilt"><b>02</b><h3>DECOMPOSE CLAIM</h3><p>Separate the literal assertion from implication, framing, emotional payload, and unstated 